WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.149
JOE: The ‘Autism act’ was the first
legislation to specifically focus on

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.350
Autism, even though the other acts do
support individuals in different ways.

00:00:09.099 --> 00:00:12.890
Because of the Act, most councils now
have a diagnosis pathway for adults,

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:17.830
a specific ‘Autism Lead’ and make sure
that every autistic person has the

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.110
right to a social care assessment,
something which was difficult for

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.910
many autistic people in the past.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.489
BETH: The ‘Fulfilling and Rewarding Lives’
strategy aimed to improve physical and

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:33.269
mental health, reduce crime and substance
misuse, reduce dependency on benefits and

00:00:33.269 --> 00:00:37.920
raise awareness amongst professionals,
also to make sure diagnostic services are

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.920
available and ensure that transitions into
adult services are managed successfully.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.719
JOE: ‘Think autism’ further built
on this by improving all aspects and

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:52.079
helping those with autism get into work,
developing skills and independence.

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:55.980
These strategies outline some of the
areas that needed to be improved,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.280
such as autism awareness training,
access to a diagnosis and assessment

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.180
and local service and support.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:06.860
BETH: Importantly, the strategies and
guidance state that a diagnosis of any

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.399
autistic spectrum condition, including
Asperger syndrome or high-functioning

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:16.050
autism, is a reason to assess somebody for
support and though it does not guarantee

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.130
services will be provided, assessment
should be carried out and look at the

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.080
person rather than their diagnosis.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.820
JOE: There is emphasis on aiming to
improve public services for people with

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:31.490
autism, such as transport, leisure,
employment and the police, to get

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.820
better at adjusting to, and meeting
the needs of, people with autism.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:39.670
Local authorities need to keep and
provide data about autism in their area,

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.420
such as the numbers of autistic people
known about, the range of need for the

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.670
support for them to live independently
and the age profile of people with autism.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:53.250
BETH: While progress has been made
since the Autism Act, there is still

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.549
much to be done in society to show that
autistic people have the same rights to

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.640
life and independence as other people.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.880
If these strategies are successful
and can change how society views

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:07.880
autism, this can lead to real
improvements in the day-to-day lives

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.850
of autistic people, as well as carers
and professionals that support them.

